  <h2 class="mt-0">A short hop up the Mansfield Road</h2>
  <p>Woodthorpe sits directly south of Arnold, and Sherwood is just beyond it towards the city. For most owners that makes Arnold an easy run up the A60, in the opposite direction to the morning traffic heading into Nottingham.</p>
  <p>Sherwood is the busy, city side of things: terraces, flats, small gardens and owners who work all sorts of hours, including plenty of shift workers. Woodthorpe is a little leafier. Either way, a day at Paws 2 Purrs swaps pavements for woods, fields and water.</p>

  <h2>More room to run than the local park</h2>
  <p>Woodthorpe Grange Park is lovely for a stroll, and Arnot Hill Park is just up the road in Arnold. But there's only so much running a dog can do on a lead between the flowerbeds. Vanessa's pack heads further out, to woodland, farm fields and water spots, where most dogs can go off lead or on a long line and properly stretch their legs.</p>
  <p>You'll get photo and video updates through the day, so you can see the difference for yourself.</p>

  <h2>What works for Woodthorpe and Sherwood owners</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Flat or small garden?</strong> A few <a href="/dog-daycare-arnold-nottingham/">daycare days</a> a week give your dog the space and company they can't get at home. Drop-off is around 7:30am and collection around 5pm.</li>
    <li><strong>Hours that change week to week?</strong> Talk to Vanessa about a mix of daycare, <a href="/dog-walking-arnold-nottingham/">walks with pick-up</a> and <a href="/dog-walking-arnold-nottingham/#pop-ins">dog pop-ins</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Away for work or a holiday?</strong> <a href="/dog-boarding-arnold-nottingham/">Home boarding</a> means sofa time and their usual sleeping spot, not a kennel run.</li>
    <li><strong>Cats in the family?</strong> <a href="/cat-sitting-arnold-nottingham/">Cat pop-ins and small animal feeds</a> are part of the service too.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Licensed, insured and long-standing</h2>
  <p>Paws 2 Purrs is licensed by Gedling Borough Council and fully insured, and Vanessa has 10 years' experience. Her regulars stay for years: Loki for around six, Reign for about four. If you're in Sherwood, part of Nottingham City rather than Gedling, nothing changes. You're welcome all the same.</p>
